  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EISP fas 2, Milj&#xf6;inftastrukturst&#xf6;d</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EISP, phase 2 Environmental Infrastructure Support Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Environmental Infrastructure Support Program (EISP) is to
build capacity with the Department for Project Management (DPM) at the Serbian
Ministry responsible for Environmental Protection to manage programming and
implementation of EU funds. The intended achievement at the end of the contribution is
that Serbia has an environmental policy and financing framework supporting EU
approximation, and capacities to manage the project pipeline to use EU funds. A
pipeline of feasable and bankable environmental infrastructure projects should have been
developed. The project is implemented by the procured consultant Brooks Hannas &amp;
Partners, in cooperation with the Serbian Ministry for Environmental Protection. 

The project started in 2016, and had a decision for cost extension in 2020.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet f&#xf6;r st&#xf6;d till milj&#xf6;infrastruktur (Enviornmental Infrastructure Support Program, EISP2) genomf&#xf6;rs av det upphandlade konsultf&#xf6;retaget Brooks Hannas &amp; Partners. Den ursprungliga budgeten var p&#xe5; 26 MSEK och projektet startade i januari 2017. En &#xf6;kning och tidsf&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning beslutades 2020. M&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttningen med projektet &#xe4;r at bist&#xe5; milj&#xf6;ministeriet med att ta f&#xf6;rbereda och genomf&#xf6;ra prioriterade milj&#xf6;investeringsprojekt vilket underl&#xe4;ttar f&#xf6;r Serbien att g&#xf6;ra de n&#xf6;dv&#xe4;ndiga investeringarna i milj&#xf6;infrastruktur med den kvalitet som EU och Serbiens EU f&#xf6;rhandlingar kr&#xe4;ver.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project Environmental Infrastructure Support Program, EISP2, is implemented by the procured consulting company Brooks Hannas &amp; Partners. The original budget was SEK 26 million and the project started in January 2017. A budget increase and extension was decided in 2020. The aim of the project is to assist the Ministry of Environmental Protection in preparing and implementing priority environmental investment projects, which facilitates for Serbia to make the necessary investments in environmental infrastructure as required by the EU and in Serbia&apos;s EU negotiations.</narrative>
  </description>
